---
import HearthNavigation from '../../components/HearthNavigation.astro';
import '../../styles/portfolio-page.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Hearth & Code project portfolio: the full working surface — Exocore Sigil, ESS, HCAN, the platform, the game, and the Ember Circuit design system." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0E1114" />
    <title>Portfolio · Hearth & Code</title>
  </head>
  <body class="portfolio-page ember-surface">
    <a class="portfolio-skip" href="#portfolio-main">Skip to portfolio</a>
    <div class="portfolio-shell">
      <HearthNavigation current="exocore" context="Project portfolio · working surface" />

      <main id="portfolio-main">
        <!-- Hero -->
        <section class="portfolio-hero" aria-labelledby="portfolio-title">
          <p class="portfolio-kicker">Working surface · 2026</p>
          <h1 id="portfolio-title">The full working surface.</h1>
          <p class="portfolio-lede">
            Eight surfaces across research, software, and knowledge architecture — each inspectable, source-grounded,
            and bounded by an honest claim vocabulary. This is what I am building, what I have built, and what I am
            exploring.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Surface cards -->
        <section class="portfolio-grid" aria-label="Project surfaces">
          <!-- 01. Exocore Sigil -->
          <article class="surface-card surface-card--sigil">
            <header>
              <span class="surface-card__num">01</span>
              <span class="surface-card__tag">Build surface</span>
            </header>
            <h2>Exocore Sigil</h2>
            <p>The inscription grammar: how bounded artifacts are written, checked, and rendered. Sigil is the surface substrate of the ESS — the four-spec decomposition that gives every artifact a grammar, a fallback, and a conformance check.</p>
            <dl class="surface-card__stats">
              <div><dt>Substrate</dt><dd>Grammar-theoretic</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Lenses</dt><dd>32</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Posture</dt><dd>Deployed (standard)</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="surface-card__link" href="/docs/portfolio/02-exocore-sigil.md">Read the Sigil brief →</a>
          </article>

          <!-- 02. ESS -->
          <article class="surface-card surface-card--ess">
            <header>
              <span class="surface-card__num">02</span>
              <span class="surface-card__tag">Four-spec foundation</span>
            </header>
            <h2>ESS</h2>
            <p>The Engineered Semantic Substrate: four substrates (TCCP, EKRP, MINC, Sigil) composing 663 bounded features. The corpus-review process and the implementation-campaign process make the work inspectable.</p>
            <dl class="surface-card__stats">
              <div><dt>Substrates</dt><dd>4</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Features</dt><dd>663</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Lenses</dt><dd>64</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Primitives</dt><dd>40</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <div class="surface-card__links">
              <a href="/docs/portfolio/01-ess-overview.md">Overview →</a>
              <a href="/docs/portfolio/04-corpus-review-process.md">Corpus review →</a>
              <a href="/docs/portfolio/05-implementation-campaign.md">Implementation campaign →</a>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- 03. HCAN -->
          <article class="surface-card surface-card--hcan">
            <header>
              <span class="surface-card__num">03</span>
              <span class="surface-card__tag">Communication medium</span>
            </header>
            <h2>HCAN</h2>
            <p>A condensed symbolic language for agent–human communication. Eight program examples, eight primitives, two protocols, and a portable envelope layer — the Hearthside Compact Agent Notation.</p>
            <dl class="surface-card__stats">
              <div><dt>Primitives</dt><dd>8</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Protocols</dt><dd>2</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Examples</dt><dd>8</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Posture</dt><dd>Deployed (/hcan)</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="surface-card__link" href="/hcan/">Explore HCAN →</a>
          </article>

          <!-- 04. Exocore Platform -->
          <article class="surface-card surface-card--platform">
            <header>
              <span class="surface-card__num">04</span>
              <span class="surface-card__tag">Platform</span>
            </header>
            <h2>Exocore</h2>
            <p>A local-first cognitive workbench: Tauri desktop app, agent host, memory layer, VS Code workspace integration, and the Pi extension for bounded review and corpus-review. The platform is where the ESS, HCAN, and Sigil surfaces meet actual work.</p>
            <dl class="surface-card__stats">
              <div><dt>Runtime</dt><dd>Tauri v2 (Rust)</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Workspace</dt><dd>VS Code integration</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Extension</dt><dd>Pi (bounded review)</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Posture</dt><dd>In development</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="surface-card__link" href="/docs/portfolio/06-exocore-platform.md">Read the platform brief →</a>
          </article>

          <!-- 05. Exocore the Game -->
          <article class="surface-card surface-card--game">
            <header>
              <span class="surface-card__num">05</span>
              <span class="surface-card__tag">Concept (not deployed)</span>
            </header>
            <h2>Exocore: The Game</h2>
            <p>A cognitive workbench game surface — the same bounded vocabulary, release pattern, and corpus-review process, applied to play. A proposal, not a deployed system.</p>
            <dl class="surface-card__stats">
              <div><dt>Posture</dt><dd>Proposal</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Source</dt><dd>Hub project 0005</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="surface-card__link" href="/docs/portfolio/12-exocore-the-game.md">Read the concept →</a>
          </article>

          <!-- 06. Palimpsest -->
          <article class="surface-card surface-card--palimpsest">
            <header>
              <span class="surface-card__num">06</span>
              <span class="surface-card__tag">Concept (not deployed)</span>
            </header>
            <h2>Palimpsest</h2>
            <p>The Last Archivist: a concept exploring layered knowledge representation and the return route. A proposal, not a deployed system.</p>
            <dl class="surface-card__stats">
              <div><dt>Posture</dt><dd>Proposal</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Source</dt><dd>Hub project 0030</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="surface-card__link" href="/docs/portfolio/13-palimpsest.md">Read the concept →</a>
          </article>

          <!-- 07. Core32 Fleet -->
          <article class="surface-card surface-card--core32">
            <header>
              <span class="surface-card__num">07</span>
              <span class="surface-card__tag">Agent fleet</span>
            </header>
            <h2>Core32</h2>
            <p>Thirty-two named specialist profiles, each with a bounded role, an input type, an output type, and a falsifier. The fleet is the agent side of the working surface.</p>
            <dl class="surface-card__stats">
              <div><dt>Profiles</dt><dd>32</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Posture</dt><dd>Deployed (standard)</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="surface-card__link" href="/docs/portfolio/08-core32-fleet.md">Read the fleet brief →</a>
          </article>

          <!-- 08. Ember Circuit -->
          <article class="surface-card surface-card--ember">
            <header>
              <span class="surface-card__num">08</span>
              <span class="surface-card__tag">Design system</span>
            </header>
            <h2>Ember Circuit</h2>
            <p>The visual language: field-950, ember-500, cream-bright. Georgia for display, system-ui for body, SF-Mono for code. The layout grammar (cover, bento-grid, step-list, comparison-rows) that gives every surface its inspectable structure.</p>
            <dl class="surface-card__stats">
              <div><dt>Tokens</dt><dd>3 primary + 5 accent</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Layouts</dt><dd>9 patterns</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Posture</dt><dd>Deployed (this page)</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a class="surface-card__link" href="/docs/portfolio/10-ember-circuit-design-system.md">Read the design system →</a>
          </article>
        </section>

        <!-- Process diagrams -->
        <section class="portfolio-process" aria-labelledby="process-title">
          <header class="portfolio-section-head">
            <div>
              <p class="portfolio-kicker">Process</p>
              <h2 id="process-title">How the work is checked.</h2>
            </div>
            <p>Two bounded processes make the work inspectable: a reading test and an action test. Each leaves a receipt.</p>
          </header>

          <div class="process-grid">
            <div class="process-card">
              <h3>Corpus review</h3>
              <p class="process-card__desc">A four-step reading test applied to every source before it enters a claim.</p>
              <ol class="process-steps">
                <li><strong>Select</strong> — choose the source by authority and relevance</li>
                <li><strong>Frame</strong> — extract the claim, the boundary, and the question</li>
                <li><strong>Read</strong> — read the full source, not a summary</li>
                <li><strong>Receipt</strong> — record the source, the digest, and the review state</li>
              </ol>
              <a class="process-card__link" href="/docs/portfolio/04-corpus-review-process.md">Full process →</a>
            </div>

            <div class="process-card">
              <h3>Implementation campaign</h3>
              <p class="process-card__desc">A five-step action test applied to every effect before it runs.</p>
              <ol class="process-steps">
                <li><strong>Plan</strong> — name the effect, the target, and the scope</li>
                <li><strong>Source</strong> — bind the source and the review state</li>
                <li><strong>Release</strong> — obtain the explicit human release</li>
                <li><strong>Preflight</strong> — check the scope and the no-touch boundaries</li>
                <li><strong>Receipt</strong> — record what changed, how, and why</li>
              </ol>
              <a class="process-card__link" href="/docs/portfolio/05-implementation-campaign.md">Full process →</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Bounded vocabulary -->
        <section class="portfolio-vocab" aria-labelledby="vocab-title">
          <header class="portfolio-section-head">
            <div>
              <p class="portfolio-kicker">Vocabulary</p>
              <h2 id="vocab-title">Eight terms, no ninth.</h2>
            </div>
            <p>Every claim in the working surface uses one of eight labels. The absence of a label is itself a defect.</p>
          </header>
          <ol class="vocab-list">
            <li><strong>source</strong> — a quoted, citable, original statement</li>
            <li><strong>evidence</strong> — an observation or measurement that supports a claim</li>
            <li><strong>inference</strong> — a reasoned conclusion with visible assumptions</li>
            <li><strong>hypothesis</strong> — an explanation awaiting a discriminating test</li>
            <li><strong>proposal</strong> — a candidate artifact awaiting disposition</li>
            <li><strong>projection</strong> — a source-derived view that cannot replace its source</li>
            <li><strong>receipt</strong> — a bounded process report, not authority for the next action</li>
            <li><strong>unknown</strong> — an explicit gap, not a silent fill</li>
          </ol>
          <a class="vocab-link" href="/docs/portfolio/09-bounded-vocabulary.md">Read the vocabulary brief →</a>
        </section>

        <!-- Reference index -->
        <section class="portfolio-references" aria-labelledby="ref-title">
          <header class="portfolio-section-head">
            <div>
              <p class="portfolio-kicker">Reference</p>
              <h2 id="ref-title">Sixteen reference documents.</h2>
            </div>
            <p>Each surface card links to a brief. These are public-safe content references, not separate routes.</p>
          </header>
          <ol class="ref-list">
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/01-ess-overview.md">ESS overview</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/02-exocore-sigil.md">Exocore Sigil</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/03-hcan-grammar.md">HCAN grammar</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/04-corpus-review-process.md">Corpus review process</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/05-implementation-campaign.md">Implementation campaign</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/06-exocore-platform.md">Exocore platform</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/07-agentic-os.md">Agentic OS</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/08-core32-fleet.md">Core32 fleet</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/09-bounded-vocabulary.md">Bounded vocabulary</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/10-ember-circuit-design-system.md">Ember Circuit design system</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/11-hub-orientation.md">Hub orientation</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/12-exocore-the-game.md">Exocore: The Game</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/13-palimpsest.md">Palimpsest</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/14-release-pattern.md">Release pattern</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/15-hub-orientation-deck.md">Hub orientation deck (r007)</a></li>
            <li><a href="/docs/portfolio/16-public-safe-boundary.md">Public-safe boundary</a></li>
          </ol>
        </section>
      </main>

      <footer class="portfolio-footer">
        <span>Hearth & Code · Hearthside Meta-Architect</span>
        <span>Public working surface · no tracking · correction welcome</span>
        <a href="#portfolio-main">Return to top ↑</a>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
